template_override": 1, "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le16ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le16ob02re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn10le16ob02re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn10le16ob02re2img01.jpg", "text": "If you were to stand in a crowded area and watch the people, what would you see? If you were to stand close to people, what would you hear? If you were to compare a picture of people on the street today with those taken 25 years ago, what would you notice? If you understood the difference could you explain how it happened?\n<br>\nTonight the Now Gallery will be displaying art documenting \"The Death of Conversation\". You don't need to forward this to me, I'll be going there anyway. I'll be the one standing in a corner watching the rest of you. While you're looking at the art - that is, if you really are looking at the art - I'll be taking note of how you interact.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn10le16ob02re2img02.jpg", "text": "Stationary cameras, mounted on the wall, will be recording people talking, texting, tweeting, posting, or taking selfies. This in turn will be feeding into large viewing screens at either end of the gallery.\n<br>\nWhat is the exhibit about? If you knew how seriously dull people were today, you would get it immediately! How sad we are! The images captured show how we look to devices, rather than to the people we are with. How long will those caught immersed in their phones remain there before they raise their heads and verbally connect?", "time": "46000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn10le16ob02re2img03.jpg", "text": "If you were at this exhibit but didn't remember it until you revisited your social media, then perhaps you, like the people on the walls are overconnected.\n<br>\nI took an online test to see where I stood compared to others in regards to being connected to the net. My meager rating of 22% said I had more time for things outside of cyberspace and preferred to connect face to face. Where do you stand?", "time": "84000", "id": 3}]}}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena"}